WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.020
Askin Axe, return to the age of myths and magic, demons and dragons.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:28.080
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.960
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:31.640
And I'm Joe.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:38.700
Astianax. Or Astanax.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.040
Or Astranax.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.640
Or Ask Ya Next.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:46.520
Question. But I don't have a question actually.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.560
I have more of a statement here.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.960
That should have been for the Essential Games list segment.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:55.200
Yeah. Well, we can still do it because creativity is dead anyway.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.660
So we'll just throw that in there at some point.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.020
Astianax. You would think that that's like the world, right?

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:04.560
That this game takes place in or something.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:08.280
Or the sword maybe that the guy controls, but he actually has an axe.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:11.380
But Astianax is the name of the hero.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:20.660
It's the name of the 16-year-old boy from Greenview High School who gets transported to this other world.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.060
So does that mean that his name was always Astianax?

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:26.420
Like even on Earth?

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.220
I mean, it seems like it.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.080
It seems like that's what they are calling.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:31.820
He recognizes that name immediately.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:33.700
Yeah. It's like, oh, yeah.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.120
I got like a Greek name.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.280
Like that's the one reference to the names.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.880
Like, yeah, my name's like some Greek shit.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.660
And it just makes you wonder, like, did they just have the name?

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.140
And they're like, we have to shoehorn the name in?

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.020
Because it doesn't mean anything else.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.580
Like, why wasn't it just like Gary's World?

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:58.740
Yeah, but yeah, this game doesn't really like seem to revolve around Greek mythology or anything any other way.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:05.380
Astianax is, yeah, he's a 16-year-old student from Earth, presumably.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.740
I mean, they don't say Earth out loud, I think.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.900
No, that's Greenview Venus.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.220
Right, right, right. Greenview High School.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:19.800
And he's been having a recurring dream in which a young woman is calling out his name.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:21.220
Astianax, Astianax.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.160
And maybe that's why he is the Chosen One.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.400
Like, he was actually supposed to be born in this other realm.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.620
And he got somehow wound up on Earth.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.040
And they're like, all right, bring him over.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:43.020
One day, while on his way to class, Astianax is suddenly transported to another dimension where he meets this fairy creature who tells him, like, yep, you gotta save the princess.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:48.240
And don't worry, because here, you're a human who has special powers.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.160
And then the game just begins.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.420
Well, you skipped a couple things.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:54.620
Sure, I skipped a couple things.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.840
But I guess what I'm saying is, like, this is all shoehorned into then, like, the regular game, right?

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:03.940
Do we really need this whole concept of boy from Earth?

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:12.500
Earth is now a little bit different because he also got transported for seemingly no reason other than being the Chosen One into this other realm?

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:19.200
Yeah, I mean, on one hand, you could just say, like, why not just start in this other realm and just be a hero of the other realm?

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.800
I guess it seems like they were trying to go for, like, this relatability to their, like, audience.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.800
Where it's like, oh, you could be just like Astianax.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.400
You're a sophomore or freshman in high school or whatever it is.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:36.600
So it's, like, just weird to have this cutscene where he's just, like, in regular clothes at a desk.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:39.200
And then, like, the rest of the game, he's, like, in armor.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.780
It's like a regular Joe kind of guy.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.820
Like, in high school, boy meets a fairy.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:54.160
A fairy tricks boy into sacrificing his life for someone he doesn't know.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:59.640
A fairy feels bad and kills herself.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.120
Boy, rescue princess.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.660
A princess invite boy to party.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.760
Boy, not happy.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.780
Boy, want, go home.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:12.040
And then boy meet girl.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.440
That's exactly, yeah, it's like that, you know, it's like Boy Meets World.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:20.040
It is. Just the slightly, slightly few extra steps.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:24.320
But, but, but, Mike, you don't like that the story exists at all.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:28.140
Well, would you be surprised if I told you that the arcade version didn't have any of this?

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:33.480
I wouldn't, but I, I'm also, like, just surprised as to, you know,

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:40.680
like, after every level, you get a little bit of this ridiculous, dumb story, and I'm here for it.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.220
Yeah, I kind of like it, too.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.820
I mean, it's, it's, it's not a good story, but it, like, it keeps me invested.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.880
Like, oh, I want to kill that purple skeleton guy.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.960
Yeah, the purple skeleton guy is kind of the worst.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.080
Yeah, it sucks.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:55.920
But, you know, like, just to get into a little nitty gritty of the story here,

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.480
you know what also sort of sucks is this fairy.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.820
Cutie. Kind of like, like you alluded to, Cutie is her name.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:04.060
She, she summons you here.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:07.400
You end up in this other world, and she's like, yeah, you're the chosen one,

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.400
and you have to save the world.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:09.400
And he's like, oh, I don't want to do it.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:12.660
And she's like, oh, sorry, like, that's the only way to get back to your world.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.360
I didn't, like, you're stuck here now.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.700
And then she, she's like, well, you know, actually, you have no choice.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.380
So it's just like, wow, that's a shitty thing to do.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.260
And then it turns out that you have to die.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:23.560
So she knew this all along.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:24.440
She's kind of the worst.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.640
It is weird, though, that the game chose that route, right?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.420
Of, like, the player character being the kind of person who would be like,

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:32.760
nah, I don't want to.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.500
Send me back to high school.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:35.920
Well, the reluctant hero.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.680
It's just like the most literal interpretation of a reluctant hero.

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:41.120
He basically says, I'm reluctant to be the hero.

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:47.360
I'm just thinking back to, back to Sean's point of, like, you know, putting it,

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:48.560
or sorry, this was your point, Joe,

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:51.620
of putting it in the viewer's lens, right?

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.280
Of, like, oh, that boy's just like me,

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.940
and he got transported to this magical world, and I'm controlling him.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.120
It's, like, weird to, you bought the game.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:05:59.500
Like, you want to go on the adventure,

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:02.080
and your character is like, nah, don't want to do it.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.920
I mean, we've talked about this concept before,

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.460
like, in a lot of Japanese games.

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:10.520
Like, they give you the option to say no to the adventure.

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:12.560
And I guess it's more,

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.940
I'm more relieved that they just didn't do that.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.940
Like, if they gave you a text box,

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:18.480
and if you could have said no,

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:21.440
even after they've already made you reluctant,

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:23.680
I'm just glad.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.900
That sort of sounds redundant, you know?

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.940
So we've got a side-scrolling action game here,

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:36.160
where the Ashton Axe character has an axe or a sword for a,

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.560
it looks like a sword with, like, some extra spikes on it.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:40.220
I'm sure there's a fancy word for that.

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:43.060
But that's his weapon of choice.

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:47.280
And the interesting thing about how they deal with this,

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.340
rather than how we've seen it in other action side-scrollers,

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:52.220
is that there is a power gauge.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:55.900
And that power gauge is something that every time you swing,

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.720
it goes back to the minimum level of the gauge.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:02.320
And then as you wait to swing again, it slowly increases.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:03.380
It does have a maximum,

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:05.620
so you can't just sit there for 20 minutes

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.160
charging up the ultimate shot.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:11.400
But that power gauge, which does fill up pretty quickly,

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:16.040
encourages you not for, like, rapid swings of the sword,

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:19.520
because you have to, it's the striking power of your weapon.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:21.160
What did we think of the power gauge?

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:22.720
I sort of liked it.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.600
So I was playing with a friend of mine,

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:28.100
and at first we were both kind of like,

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:32.400
oh, this is stupid. And I think that he might have continued to have that opinion

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.660
the whole time we played.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:35.460
I started, it started to grow on me.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.560
It really started to give me, like, the feeling of, like,

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:38.580
oh, I have the choice between,

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:41.200
it's a very organic way of giving you the choice

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.920
between a power attack and a speed attack.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:46.040
I thought it was interesting, like,

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.280
the, it almost feels like a very rudimentary version

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:53.200
of, like, a FromSoft, like, stamina gauge.

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:56.020
Like, you know, there's stamina management in those games.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:58.300
If you run out of stamina, you just can't act.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:01.960
But it's not so much that in this game.

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:04.780
It's more so if you just spam,

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:06.420
you're going to do very little damage.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:09.760
So it's sort of, I'm sure there's some,

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:13.400
if you ran the numbers, there is a trade-off

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:17.660
that if you do wait a full second,

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:20.340
like, there is more damage than you could have done

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:23.840
in the hits you could have made in that second otherwise.

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.300
So I'm sure there's something going on there

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:29.800
that makes being more patient a better idea.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:32.160
But once you get up to a certain level,

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.720
like, thankfully, you're never punished.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:39.880
Like, you get these upgrades

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:43.420
that give you a larger power gauge,

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:48.040
and that just makes your full-powered shot more powerful.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:52.660
But then it takes five seconds to fill the whole thing.

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:57.460
So you're never really punished by getting stronger.

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:59.800
Because if it was just, like, a percentage thing,

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:02.460
that would actually be a net negative.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:06.660
So I think it's, like, it's not a perfectly implemented system

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:09.620
because at a certain point it becomes,

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:14.460
it's just not feasible to use it correctly.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:17.540
But it's still a fun idea.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:18.940
At least it's a unique idea.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:21.460
Yeah, I agree with you.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.380
It's a unique idea because, like,

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:26.720
it feels like they wanted it to have more strategy,

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:31.480
like, that you should treat these individual combats

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.500
with the enemies as, you know,

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.160
like one-on-one sword duels

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:37.620
where you don't just want to spam your attack button

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.860
at the enemy and take damage

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.100
while you're giving damage.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:43.000
Like, you want to build up your power meter,

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:44.060
choose to strike,

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:46.580
make sure that when you strike you actually hit

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:48.380
because, well, you were, you know,

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.140
you were delaying your attack otherwise.

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:51.700
So you want to make sure that you land it.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:54.540
But it doesn't, the game that they built

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:55.780
doesn't really, like,

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:59.000
encourage that idea too much

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.200
because a lot of times,

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.780
you know, specifically in the stages,

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.540
like, you better want to fight all of these monsters

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.840
because these monsters will stay on the screen

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:10.260
as long as you'll carry them.

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:12.760
Like, yes, they can sometimes fall into pits

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:16.100
or, you know,

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.000
if you walk far enough away,

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:19.160
you might think that they're gone,

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:20.460
but they're not. They'll,

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:21.440
they'll stay with you

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:24.320
and they'll kind of cause this slowdown in the game too.

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:26.300
But, but,

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:27.660
you know, it's not one of those games

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:28.500
where you just, like,

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:29.620
choose your fights.

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:31.880
It's like, you better want to fight every single enemy

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:35.100
and so therefore, you don't really have the luxury of like,

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:36.600
oh, I'll just wait around

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:37.440
for my,

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:39.340
my sword to fully charge up.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:40.500
But, granted, again,

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.620
it doesn't matter. They didn't make the sword charging something like,

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:46.160
you have to wait for the sword to be fully charged

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.180
in order to attack.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:48.400
Now, that would suck.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:50.140
That would be a really bad game

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:51.780
and discourage combat.

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:53.340
Instead, it's just that

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:56.180
the amount of damage your sword does

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:58.040
is based on that power meter.

00:10:58.460 --> 00:10:59.640
Yeah, and to be clear too,

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:01.360
to anyone who hasn't, who hasn't played it,

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:03.060
we're not talking like,

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.700
we're not talking like 10 seconds to power up.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:06.980
I mean, it takes longer,

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:08.400
the higher you want the power to get,

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.320
but it powers up, you know,

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:11.480
I would say within a second,

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:13.500
it powers up to almost,

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:14.960
to max for most of the time,

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:15.900
unless you're like really powerful,

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:17.220
then maybe like a second and a half.

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:21.340
I think it gets to a point where it is like five seconds

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:22.880
to refill the whole thing.

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:25.380
I feel like it was,

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:26.740
I mean, maybe like two seconds.

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:28.560
I don't know, five seconds feels like that's like a,

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:29.860
that would be to me.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:30.920
I guess maybe also,

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:34.100
it depends on how many enemies are on the screen,

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:36.900
because everything, you get the frame drops.

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:37.760
Yeah.

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:40.240
And the power meter is worth something,

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:43.920
because since it determines how powerful your strike is,

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:46.380
even the early enemies in this game,

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.520
some of the first skeletons you fight,

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.800
I wouldn't describe them as sponges,

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:52.540
but it is surprising that they take,

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:55.180
you know, if you're swinging rapidly,

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:57.780
they take quite a number of hits to take down.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:01.700
And that's surprising for like a first level enemy in a game.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:04.920
Yeah. I think that that's kind of like what you learn early on.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.460
I mean, you sort of touched on this earlier.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:09.440
Like the game doesn't, doesn't really like encourage like,

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:12.100
Hey, either be a fast warrior or a strong warrior.

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:14.600
Like it's clearly better to use the,

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.400
the, the strong attacks.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:17.700
I think you learn that early,

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:19.660
learn that you got to get into the rhythm to,

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:21.240
of like using strong attacks.

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:22.900
Cause yeah, it'll be like those skeletons that take like,

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:27.860
take like 12 hits to kill a skeleton or like two full power hits.

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:29.400
Well, there's also,

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:34.560
I mean, it's definitely better to be a power hitter when you're surrounded by enemies.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:37.200
But if you've only got one or two on the screen,

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:43.400
uh, you're kind of balancing whether you want to like just stun lock and,

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:44.740
and do it that way.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:47.020
Kind of protect yourself with the,

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:48.440
with the enemy being stunned.

00:12:49.220 --> 00:12:50.780
Um, so there's,

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:54.240
there's, there's two different ways to go about it.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:57.360
Yeah, I guess I shouldn't say there are reasons definitely to use the,

